UGOPICK® — From Employee Voice to Public-Sector Intelligence and Action

Vision: To make the collective voice, knowledge, experience, and capabilities of public-sector employees a meaningful driver of organizational learning, collaboration, and innovation.
UGOPICK® can be envisioned as more than a polling tool. Polling provides the starting point: a simple, accessible way for employees to express opinions, share experiences, identify challenges, and signal what matters to them. The longer-term ambition is to explore how those individual signals can be connected, understood, shared, and translated into meaningful improvements across public-sector organizations.
At its heart, UGOPICK® is about unlocking a resource that every public institution possesses but may not fully mobilize: the collective intelligence of the people who make public services work.
This vision positions UGOPICK® as a potential foundation for a new kind of public-sector employee-voice platform — one that connects people and perspectives, helps organizations discover knowledge and expertise, and creates pathways from employee input to organizational action.
The ambition is not simply to give employees a voice. It is to explore how that voice can become more visible, more connected, more useful, and ultimately more influential in shaping the way public organizations learn, collaborate, and improve.

